# FOMO: Figuring Out Mislabeled Omics

This is the R package for *Deng et al. 2026, A scalable framework for
automated relabeling of mislabeled multi-omics samples*.

## Abstract for *Deng et al. 2026*

Mislabels, errors linking samples to incorrect identities, inevitably
occur in large multi-omics datasets during collection and data
generation. Mislabels dilute statistical power, bias results, and more
importantly jeopardize participants’ informed consent by preventing
correct removal of withdrawn individuals’ data from analysis and
public release. While existing methods determine identity concordance
from genetic data, no scalable, flexible tool exists that leverages
this information to resolve mislabels. We present Figuring Out
Mislabeled Omics (FOMO), which integrates genotype-derived matches and
sample labels into mislabel networks to automatically relabel at
scale. FOMO performed well in extensive simulations, demonstrating
scalability up to 100,000 samples while maintaining near-perfect
accuracy up to 20% mislabeling rate. In public multi-omics cohorts,
FOMO achieved relabeling accuracy equal to or better than manual
correction in a fraction of the time while identifying and correcting
complex mislabeling events including some missed by manual review.
FOMO is, to our knowledge, the first scalable and accurate
computational solver that integrates label metadata with genotype
information to detect and correct complex mislabeling in large
multi-omics datasets.

## Installation

You can install the package from Github using:

```R
remotes::install_github("BeckmannLab/FOMO")
```
